**Story & Context:** At 124 BPM, Aiko opens with one sustained shō cluster built around open fifth implications and a close suspended-second tension. Sizwe programs a two-kick gqom cell during EXHALE, then removes every low hit at TURN. As INHALE stabilizes, one displaced low tom enters before the kick returns. Reina adds a single prepared-piano fifth only at SETTLE. Thabo places one dry woodblock hit on every second breath reversal. Mikael remains silent until the first Vacuum Bar, where the drums, piano, and all electric low end disappear while the shō crosses from exhale to inhale alone. His bass-trombone pedal enters after the new breath direction stabilizes. The track’s hook is the repeated sensation that the chord never changes but the room’s weight changes every time the lungs reverse.

